+This timeline is a historical projection of records. Chronicle does not perform
+the update. For a consequential transition the applicable sequence is:
+
+Authorization → Execution → Observation → Evidence → Verification
+→ VerificationReceipt → Exact-parent applicability check
+→ World Kernel CAS atomic commit → Post-commit outcome delivery.
+
+The World Kernel CAS boundary makes the resulting authoritative World version,
+immutable WORLD_COMMIT_RECEIPT and durable committed-event delivery intent
+visible all-or-none. Actual delivery occurs afterward; a timeline entry or
+Chronicle persistence receipt does not represent delivery completion or commit
+authority.
+
